1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,848
Part four.

2
00:00:01,277 --> 00:00:02,322
The one number.

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,851
Damodaran's first rule of corporate finance:

4
00:00:06,339 --> 00:00:08,731
young companies that aren't making money shouldn't borrow.

5
00:00:09,091 --> 00:00:10,600
Anthropic, he says,

6
00:00:10,832 --> 00:00:12,852
broke it by signing hundreds of billions in

7
00:00:12,934 --> 00:00:15,604
compute commitments without the earnings to back them.

8
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:17,740
What buys time is cash.

9
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,354
After the IPO,

10
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,176
he expects about $200 billion,

11
00:00:21,664 --> 00:00:23,255
enough to cover the next two or three

12
00:00:23,289 --> 00:00:24,462
years of those bills.

13
00:00:24,822 --> 00:00:27,481
But only if revenue roughly doubles every year

14
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:28,409
in the near term.

15
00:00:28,897 --> 00:00:31,521
That's the one number he says drives everything.

16
00:00:31,950 --> 00:00:33,355
If revenue comes in,

17
00:00:33,436 --> 00:00:34,504
profits come,

18
00:00:34,864 --> 00:00:36,315
the commitments get paid,

19
00:00:36,397 --> 00:00:37,674
and the risk goes away.

20
00:00:38,103 --> 00:00:39,021
If it doesn't,

21
00:00:39,218 --> 00:00:40,867
everything else falls apart.

22
00:00:41,435 --> 00:00:43,606
Host Ed Elson pointed out that growth was

23
00:00:43,676 --> 00:00:47,530
already slowing, from 47% a quarter toward 15

24
00:00:47,611 --> 00:00:48,738
to 25%.

25
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:51,071
Damodaran blames competition:

26
00:00:51,524 --> 00:00:54,717
OpenAI underpricing, and cheaper open models.

27
00:00:55,564 --> 00:00:57,132
Most businesses don't need Claude,

28
00:00:57,178 --> 00:00:57,759
he says.

29
00:00:58,281 --> 00:00:59,279
It's overkill.

30
00:01:00,115 --> 00:01:02,855
His advice: build models powerful enough,

31
00:01:03,099 --> 00:01:04,261
but not too powerful.

32
00:01:04,597 --> 00:01:06,455
And even if AI helps cure diseases,

33
00:01:06,478 --> 00:01:07,175
he warns,

34
00:01:07,662 --> 00:01:09,497
the value may flow to all of us,

35
00:01:10,170 --> 00:01:12,004
not to Anthropic's shareholders.

36
00:01:12,678 --> 00:01:14,535
So why hasn't he written it off?
